# cut-pins.env — the identity of the chain this fleet joins, in ONE place.
#
# Sourced by testnet/join.sh and testnet/join-testnet-sync-node.sh. Nothing here
# is a secret; every value is public chain identity. Do not put credentials in
# this file — it is committed.
#
# WHY A SEPARATE FILE
# -------------------
# These constants were previously inlined at their use sites, and a constant
# with two copies is a constant that drifts. core4#2705 is that failure in the
# live cut: docs/security/GENESIS_CUT_RUNBOOK.md step 1 STILL declares the freeze
# at 51eb1a4a — the cut has since moved 51eb1a4a -> 67d07852 -> 23e8d62a -> deb5a3c5
# and the runbook followed neither. Its own abort check prints MAIN MOVED if run
# today. That is the drift this file exists to prevent, still unfixed in core4.
#
# So changing the cut commit must be a ONE-LINE EDIT HERE, not a hunt through
# two scripts at 2am.
#
# CHANGING A VALUE
# ----------------
# Edit the line, commit, and re-run the join. Both scripts read this at runtime
# and fail loudly on a mismatch rather than silently building or joining the
# wrong thing. Any override is announced.

# ############################################################################
# 2026-10-0x IN-PLACE HOTFIX B3.1 (owner ruling 2026-10-02 21:50Z). NOT a
# genesis cut: the chain, genesis hash, chain id and network id are unchanged.
#   WRFCOIN_CUT_CORE4_COMMIT = fe8b3191b6346ae17a5517b9ba21bdb33bab8c42 (was 65134a64492135b6ac81344dd0d2edd8dfaf1309, B3)
#     B3.1 = B3 plus ONLY the Stake/Unstake admission and relay refusal
#     (core4 hotfix/b3.1-stake-refusal). Same PROTOCOL_VERSION 3 and checkpoint
#     format 10, so a node can go back to the B3 image without a volume copy.
#   Rolled out before block 33000; owner steps in the workspace plan
#   docs/plans/overnight-2026-09-24/b31-hotfix-steps/.
# ############################################################################

# ############################################################################
# 2026-10-08 ROLLING SWAP r20.3. NOT a genesis cut: the chain, genesis hash,
# chain id and network id are unchanged.
#   WRFCOIN_CUT_CORE4_COMMIT = 620902bf7b01cf09b11b2bb0ff5a22571e7cb694 (was fe8b3191b6346ae17a5517b9ba21bdb33bab8c42, B3.1)
#     core4 main after #3319 (format 11 owner ledger, owner-tx routes,
#     registration v2). All three nodes passed the version gate (tag and
#     revision label) on 2026-10-08. The release gate requires this to equal
#     WRFCOIN_RC_CORE4_COMMIT in release-pins.env. The station features stay
#     unscheduled. Owner steps: docs/plans/overnight-2026-09-24/r20-3-swap/.
# ############################################################################

# ############################################################################
# 2026-09-29 IN-PLACE UPGRADE B3 (core4#3277 S5 #3368, infra#774). NOT a
# genesis cut: the chain, genesis hash, chain id and network id are unchanged.
#   WRFCOIN_CUT_CORE4_COMMIT = 65134a64492135b6ac81344dd0d2edd8dfaf1309
#     (was 9ef92a235143…, rc0926). B3 = PROTOCOL_VERSION 3 with the
#      schedule_extension bootstrap at H_ENABLE 29800 on chain 777.
# Before H_ENABLE, B3 produces and validates blocks exactly as rc0926 did
# (S5's parity test); it writes checkpoint format 10, so a node that has run
# B3 cannot go back to rc0926 without its pre-B3 volume copy. Joiners
# (join.sh) now build this commit. Rollout: core4
# docs/operations/SCHEDULE_EXTENSION_ROLLOUT_RUNBOOK.md (R0-R7).
# ############################################################################

# ############################################################################
# 2026-09-26 IN-PLACE UPGRADE rc0926 (infra#774). NOT a genesis cut: the chain,
# genesis hash, chain id and network id below are unchanged.
#   WRFCOIN_CUT_CORE4_COMMIT = 9ef92a235143aa683cf9b90ddc86ae679324f8fc
#     (was 72a993552d18…, the 2026-09-13 cut binary; the fleet has run
#      8a0e2bfbb9b8 since 2026-09-25 and moves to 9ef92a235 in rc0926)
# Evidence: the candidate replays the live chain from genesis to h23233 and
# reproduces live CT101's state root byte-identically (docs repo
# plans/overnight-2026-09-24/redeploy-runbook-rc0926.md §0). Joiners
# (join.sh) now build this commit, i.e. the fleet's binary, which replays
# the same chain. "Cut" in the variable name is historical (infra#774).
# ############################################################################

# ############################################################################
# 2026-09-13 RE-CUT (#2708 / #2035 "same window"). New fresh-genesis cut.
#   WRFCOIN_CUT_CORE4_COMMIT = 72a993552d18e60862c92a318116a1a761884fc9
#   WRFCOIN_CUT_GENESIS_HASH = 6ad436386cfc6c746146f6ef2f9d32ddb7a93f18efd3635606abd27c9ca17db8
#   infra cut commit         = c3ce814cf596db3754b7f8b3c4eaec90861f1b4e
# Supersedes the 2026-09-10 cut (core4 8d29ea85b, genesis 805efc97…) recorded in
# the blocks below, which are retained as dated history. A genesis cut starts a
# FRESH chain: the old values now name chains that no longer run.
# ############################################################################

# --- core4 revision the node binary is built from (infra#764) --------------
#
# AUTHORITATIVE: core4 docs/plans/2026-09-10-cut-preflight.md (header + A1),
# the 2026-09-10 cut: three genesis producers (mango-mini re-seated, #3088),
# Phase B producer settlement in. Frozen bundle ec3bad38… at 10,342 entries,
# control pair 67d07852 -> db1b5c63…/10,229 reproduced. Supersedes 8f072b31
# (the 2026-08-28 rollout) and every earlier cut listed below.
#
# WARNING for anyone cross-checking against the in-repo runbook:
# core4 docs/security/GENESIS_CUT_RUNBOOK.md is STALE and still names the
# superseded values — line 678 pins 51eb1a4a, line 684 expects the RETIRED
# archive hash 2cd34aa6…, and line 691's abort check compares against 51eb1a4a
# and so prints "*** MAIN MOVED ***" today even though the freeze is intact.
# Prefer §9 of the freeze declaration. Tracked in core4#2705, whose headline
# claim (that the cut commit is undecided) has been retracted — the runbook
# staleness is what survives of it.
WRFCOIN_CUT_CORE4_COMMIT=620902bf7b01cf09b11b2bb0ff5a22571e7cb694

# --- Which chain this fleet joins ------------------------------------------
#
# All verified against the live chain on 2026-08-04 via /network/info on CT 101
# (chain_height 46324, peer_count 1, sync_status synced). If the cut is retaken
# at a different commit (core4#2705), the genesis hash changes with it and this
# is the line to edit.
#
# The node returns genesis_hash 0x-prefixed; store it unprefixed and let the
# scripts normalise, so there is one representation here.
#
# ############################################################################
# SET 2026-08-05, AFTER THE CUT. There is a chain to join again.
# ############################################################################
#
# Read from the cutting node's own /network/info once block 1 was mined — which
# is exactly what the previous revision of this block instructed:
#
#   {"chain_height":1,"chain_id":"777","network_id":"testnet",
#    "genesis_hash":"0x805efc973fe50829ae2abf7c73bde0a5ed8511f3dfa97ff50a86615703442625",
#    "local_peer_id":"12D3KooWMM7ukbQrn4BH2SjSNvyvAW2SaKUkHmDRng9KnifgYeWr"}
#
# Cut at 2026-08-05 16:19:34 UTC on the 8f072b31 binary. Block 1 carries the
# three oracle registrations plus the coinbase (transaction_count 4) and declares
# oracle_quorum 2.
#
# This REPLACES a3301def68ac695636e90d7a66f83e6144a74da0ed5f234a298b73906a437658,
# the genesis of the retired 47,775-block testnet. Do not restore that value — a
# genesis cut starts a FRESH chain, so it now names a chain that no longer runs.
#
# Between the retirement and this line the variable was deliberately unset, so
# that `join-testnet-sync-node.sh:67`'s `:?` refused by name rather than verify
# against a dead chain. That window is now closed.
WRFCOIN_CUT_GENESIS_HASH=6ad436386cfc6c746146f6ef2f9d32ddb7a93f18efd3635606abd27c9ca17db8

# chain_id is a STRING everywhere it is compared. A bare 777 in JSON is a
# number and fails an exact-equality test with no coercion.
WRFCOIN_CUT_CHAIN_ID=777
WRFCOIN_CUT_NETWORK_ID=testnet

# Reference node. peer id verified equal to the node's own local_peer_id, and
# TCP 9000 verified reachable over the tailnet, on 2026-08-04.
# Public template: obtain the published address; pass --bootstrap when joining.
WRFCOIN_CUT_BOOTSTRAP="/ip4/<N5_PUBLIC_IP>/tcp/9000/p2p/12D3KooWMM7ukbQrn4BH2SjSNvyvAW2SaKUkHmDRng9KnifgYeWr"

# --- Trusted snapshot-ingest signer (infra#1080, ceremony C4) ---------------
#
# The ed25519 public key core4 accepts on signed /state/snapshot ingest. It is
# the key in PIV slot 9C of YubiKey #35278470 on the N5 producer, i.e. the only
# host that serves signed snapshots. Nothing else is trusted: the per-volume
# SoftHSM snapshot keys on other hosts are deliberately NOT listed.
#
# Adopted, not re-keyed: on 2026-09-27 the token attested this key (so it was
# generated on-device; an imported key cannot be attested), the attestation
# chains to Yubico Attestation Root 1, and the policy is PIN once / touch never.
# The attestation and the offline re-verification commands are in
# testnet/ceremony/snapshot-signer-9c/ (README.md);
# testnet/tests/test_snapshot_signer_attestation.sh re-checks that this line
# equals the attested key.
#
# EFFECT OF THIS LINE. join-testnet-sync-node.sh copies it into a joiner's .env,
# and check-env-completeness.sh now ERRORs on any host whose
# WRFCOIN_SNAPSHOT_TRUSTED_SIGNERS is absent or not set-equal to it. That is the
# intended drift detector: a host fails the gate until its .env is updated and
# the node recreated (the node reads the list only at start).
#
# ROTATION: comma-separated "<old>,<new>" for one deploy cycle only, then drop
# <old>. On loss or suspicion, remove the key here and from every host FIRST.
WRFCOIN_CUT_SNAPSHOT_TRUSTED_SIGNERS=14f423fa3894a4ccc37730f4c588e41e8bb1ed38dc7280685e78c02c36a748e9

# --- Genesis faucet address (core4#3361 option B, owner ruling 2026-09-28) ---
#
# The address block 1 records as the ADR-003 faucet sink (core4#3039). It is a
# CUT-ONLY input: required for every future cut of a chain whose emission table
# funds a faucet slice (chain id 777), never for mainnet (0 bps).
#
# DELIBERATELY EMPTY. This file describes the chain the fleet runs NOW, and the
# live chain 777 was cut on 2026-09-13 with no faucet address; pinning one here
# would claim something false about it. check-env-completeness.sh WARNs about
# that until option A binds one in place, and core4
# scripts/gather-cut-prerequisites.py lists it as BLOCKING. Fill this line WHEN
# PREPARING THE NEXT CUT, then run on the cutting host only:
#   ./check-env-completeness.sh --cut
# which ERRORs unless the host's WRFCOIN_GENESIS_FAUCET_ADDRESS equals it and a
# compose file passes it to the node. Format: 0x + 40 hex, not the zero address.
WRFCOIN_CUT_GENESIS_FAUCET_ADDRESS=
